{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791194013,"nonce":"HMBSMg/5iajyz9RZGEQu19amzWs=","title":"threads suite aborts under hybrid and jit when run whole: uncaught throw in testThreadRunWithEventLoop","message":"The official Haxe `threads` suite, run as ONE process (`ash --mode hybrid bin/threads.hl` from tests/threads), aborts about 230ms in under hybrid and jit:\n\n    Running cases.TestEvents...\n        testThreadRunWithEventLoop\n    [ash] uncaught exception: instance of haxe.ValueException (0x300038380)\n    hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting\n\nExit 134 (SIGABRT), 3/3 runs. `--mode interp` runs the whole suite to \"ALL TESTS OK\". Every case passes when isolated (conformance --isolate: hybrid and jit 1069/1069), so the failure needs state left by earlier cases in the same process.\n\nNot recent: ash 0.1.4 (~/.ash/bin/ash) aborts the same way, as do 8e2c60f and the shared-module change on top of it.\n\nCI never sees it: conformance.yml runs interp,aot,wasm,wasm-fibers, and the whole-suite hybrid row only appears in a local `--modes hybrid,jit` run.\n\nReproduce: scripts/haxe_conformance.py --modes hybrid --suites threads, or run the built bin/threads.hl from the suite's tests/threads directory.","files":null}]}